 \\pi_L = \\frac{110Q_L - Q_L^2}{2} - 11Q_L\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = \\frac{110Q_L - Q_L^2 - 22Q_L}{2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = \\frac{88Q_L - Q_L^2}{2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = 44Q_L - \\frac{Q_L^2}{2}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Maximize Firm L's Profit**:\n   - Take the derivative of \\( \\pi_L \\) with respect to \\( Q_L \\) and set it to zero:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{d\\pi_L}{dQ_L} = 44 - Q_L = 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     Q_L = 44\n     \\]\n\n7. **Calculate Firm L's Profit**:\n   - Substitute \\( Q_L = 44 \\) back into the profit function:\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = 44 \\cdot 44 - \\frac{44^2}{2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = 1936 - 968\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\pi_L = 968\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, firm L's profit in the subgame-perfect equilibrium is **968**.","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"exact_match","expected":"1458","extract":"(-?\\d[\\d,]*)(?:\\.0+(?!\\d))?"},"timing":{"wall_sec":19.781,"prompt_tokens":108,"generation_tokens":797,"ttft_ms":224,"prefill_ms":224,"decode_ms":19526,"source":"client","cached_prompt_tokens":10}},{"item_id":"stackelberg_leader_profit_s1","prompt_name":"stackelberg_leader_profit_s1","family":"stackelberg","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"To find the subgame-perfect equilibrium and firm L's profit, we need to work through the problem step-by-step.\n\n1. **Inverse Demand Function:**\n   \\( P = 101 - Q \\)\n   where \\( Q \\) is the total output, \\( Q = Q_L + Q_F \\).\n\n2. **Marginal Costs:**\n   - Firm L: \\( MC_L = 11 \\)\n   - Firm F: \\( MC_F = 17 \\)\n\n3. **Firm L's Profit Maximization:**\n   Firm L chooses its quantity \\( Q_L \\) first. Firm L's profit is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = P \\cdot Q_L - MC_L \\cdot Q_L = (101 - Q) \\cdot Q_L - 11 \\cdot Q_L\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( Q = Q_L + Q_F \\):\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = (101 - Q_L - Q_F) \\cdot Q_L - 11 \\cdot Q_L\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 101 Q_L - Q_L^2 - Q_L Q_F - 11 Q_L\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 90 Q_L - Q_L^2 - Q_L Q_F\n   \\]\n\n4. **Firm F's Reaction Function:**\n   Firm F observes \\( Q_L \\) and chooses \\( Q_F \\) to maximize its profit:\n   \\[\n   \\pi_F = P \\cdot Q_F - MC_F \\cdot Q_F = (101 - Q) \\cdot Q_F - 17 \\cdot Q_F\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( Q = Q_L + Q_F \\):\n   \\[\n   \\pi_F = (101 - Q_L - Q_F) \\cdot Q_F - 17 \\cdot Q_F\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_F = 101 Q_F - Q_L Q_F - Q_F^2 - 17 Q_F\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_F = 84 Q_F - Q_L Q_F - Q_F^2\n   \\]\n\n   To maximize \\( \\pi_F \\), take the derivative with respect to \\( Q_F \\) and set it to zero:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{d\\pi_F}{dQ_F} = 84 - Q_L - 2 Q_F = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   Q_F = \\frac{84 - Q_L}{2}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Substitute \\( Q_F \\) back into Firm L's Profit:**\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 90 Q_L - Q_L^2 - Q_L \\left( \\frac{84 - Q_L}{2} \\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 90 Q_L - Q_L^2 - \\frac{84 Q_L - Q_L^2}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 90 Q_L - Q_L^2 - 42 Q_L + \\frac{Q_L^2}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 48 Q_L - \\frac{Q_L^2}{2}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Maximize Firm L's Profit:**\n   Take the derivative of \\( \\pi_L \\) with respect to \\( Q_L \\) and set it to zero:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{d\\pi_L}{dQ_L} = 48 - Q_L = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   Q_L = 48\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate Firm L's Profit:**\n   Substitute \\( Q_L = 48 \\) back into the profit function:\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 48 \\cdot 48 - \\frac{48^2}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 2304 - 1152\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi_L = 1152\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, firm L's profit in the subgame-perfect equilibrium is **1152**.","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"exact_match","expected":"1152","extract":"(-?\\d[\\d,]*)(?:\\.0+(?!\\d))?"},"timing":{"wall_sec":22.118,"prompt_tokens":108,"generation_tokens":891,"ttft_ms":221,"prefill_ms":221,"decode_ms":21865,"source":"client","cached_prompt_tokens":25}},{"item_id":"stackelberg_chain#1","prompt_name":"stackelberg_chain#1","family":"stackelberg","parent_item_id":"stackelberg_chain","turn":1,"prior